r. Its far side reveals a calm sunlit version of the same observatory, while the current world shakes beneath orange firelight, falling dust, loose papers, and cracking ceiling structures. A medium two-shot frames a fictional thirty-year-old man with short black hair, a dust-stained dark-gray long coat, and a small cut on his cheek, facing a fictional twenty-eight-year-old woman with short brown hair and a dark-blue coat. She grips his wrist with both hands and refuses to enter the rift. The camera pushes toward them with small amplitude at slow speed while the background destruction remains softly out of focus.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.500, the camera cuts to an 85mm close-up of the woman (S1). Blue light from the rift moves across her tearful eyes while warm sparks glow behind her. Dust and a single tear mark her face; she maintains eye contact with the man and says in a quiet, urgent English voice: <d>[English] We still have time.</d> Her lips close after the final word as she tightens her grip on his wrist. Keep her performance controlled and realistic, never melodramatic.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:05.500, the camera cuts to a close-up of the man (S2). The unstable blue rift is reflected clearly in his eyes. He takes one restrained breath, looks briefly toward the collapsing ceiling, then returns his gaze to the woman. With a low, steady English voice that almost breaks at the end, he replies: <d>[English] Only one of us does.</d> His lips close, and his expression settles into quiet resolve rather than panic.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:08.500, the camera cuts to a tight two-shot. The man gently holds the woman's face with both hands and presses his forehead against hers. For one brief second, the surrounding destruction becomes visually secondary and the camera holds nearly still on their breathing and eye contact. A violent structural impact shakes the chamber. Without warning, the man turns his body, keeps one hand behind her shoulder, and pushes her backward through the blue time rift. The camera trucks sideways with them, staying at medium-close distance and preserving both faces.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:11.000, the camera cuts to an extreme close-up of their hands. The woman has crossed into the quiet sunlit observatory and immediately turns back. Their palms align on opposite sides of the semi-transparent energy membrane, fingers matching but unable to touch. Blue energy ripples outward from the point between their hands while the rift rapidly contracts. Their hands remain anatomically correct and physically separated by the membrane.\n\n[Shot 6] At 00:13.000, the camera cuts to a close-up of the woman on the safe side. She stares through the shrinking rift, breathing unevenly. Over her shoulder, the man stands alone in the amber-lit collapsing observatory, softly out of focus, offering one small restrained smile. The rift closes to a thin blue line and disappears without an explosion. The final blue reflection fades inside the woman's tear-filled eye as the camera pushes in with very small amplitude at slow speed. End at exactly 00:15.000. No additional dialogue, no subtitles, no on-screen text, no logos, no watermark, no famous actor likeness, no gore, no duplicated characters, no malformed hands, and no exaggerated crying.\n\noverall_soundscape: Deep structural groans, distant impacts, falling debris, fluttering paper, low electrical resonance from the time rift, restrained breathing, and subtle fabric movement surround the dialogue. When the woman crosses the rift, the chaotic ambience becomes muffled and distant, followed by a soft energy pulse and near silence as the portal closes.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Sparse piano notes and sustained low cello begin slowly, joined by restrained brass and deep cinematic pulses as the observatory collapses. The music rises during the forced separation, then drops to a single sustained string note and a faint piano tone for the final close-up."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value",